{"name":"Endo","hex":"#5da464","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Endo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Japanese."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Endo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Endo (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Endo was a four-piece nu metal group from Miami, Florida. They formed in 1995, released two major record label albums in 2001 and 2003, and worked on songs for a third before disbanding in 2007. In 2012, the band got back together with Gil, Eli and Joel, with their new bass player, Derek Gormley. Recording on their new album began early in 2013 with B-Team Records in Miami, Florida. The album was released in July 2013."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/40/Endo_band_%22songs_for_the_restless%22_booklet.png/330px-Endo_band_%22songs_for_the_restless%22_booklet.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endo_(band)"},{"title":"Endō","blocks":[{"text":"Endō, Endo, Endou or Endoh is the 38th most common Japanese surname. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"items":["Ado Endoh , Japanese actress","Akari Endo, Dominican-Japanese actress","Akifumi Endō , Japanese voice actor","Akihiro Endō , Japanese footballer","Akira Endo (disambiguation), multiple people","Arata Endo , Japanese architect","Aya Endō , Japanese voice actress","Ayumi Endō , Japanese artist","Chujiro Endo , Japanese baseball player","Genichi Endo , Japanese footballer","Harry Endo (1922–2009), American actor","Hiroki Endo , Japanese manga artist","Hiroyuki Endo , Japanese badminton player","Issei Endō , Japanese baseball player","Jun Endo , Japanese women's footballer","Junki Endo , Japanese footballer","Kaname Endo , Japanese actor","Keisuke Endo , Japanese footballer","Keita Endo , Japanese footballer","Kenichi Endō , Japanese actor and writer","Kenny Endo, American taiko musician","Endō Kinsuke , Japanese statesman","Kosuke Endo